ess than one year old is called a leveret. A group of hares may be called either a husk or a down."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-hare"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hare"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Spanish cuisine","cuisine/spanish-cuisine",[["Andrajos","dish/andrajos"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Cod as food","ingredient/cod-as-food"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Pasta","ingredient/pasta"],["Rabbit","ingredient/rabbit"],["Rabbit meat","ingredient/rabbit-meat"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"]]}]},"dish/bretelli":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/bretelli","n":"Bretelli","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Bretelli was a restaurant in Weert in the Netherlands from 1999 to its closing in 2018. It was a quality restaurant that was awarded one Michelin star in 2007 and retained that rating until present. In the period 2002-2006 the restaurant held a Bib Gourmand."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-bretelli"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bretelli"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine"],["New Caledonian cuisine","cuisine/new-caledonian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pardon Your French","ref":"site/pardonyourfrench-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pardonyourfrench.com","note":"Audrey Le Goff, a French cook, shares classic and regional French home recipes.","url":"https://pardonyourfrench.com","suggested":true},{"name":"La Cuisine de Géraldine","ref":"site/lacuisinedegeraldine-fr","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"lacuisinedegeraldine.fr","note":"French home cooking blog by Géraldine Leverd, also author of The New French Kitchen.","url":"https://lacuisinedegeraldine.fr/en/about-us","suggested":true},{"name":